From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: Use a flexible array member for QoS action frames

receive_qos_action_frame() forwards received QoS action frames through a
WAPP event. Although frame length is checked against event capacity,
FORTIFY treats frm[0] as a zero-size field and reports a field-spanning
write when frame data is copied.

A flexible array member describes variable-length frame storage to the
compiler. Copies remain bounded by the existing event capacity check.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/include/qos.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/qos.h
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ struct GNU_PACKED wapp_qos_action_frame
 	u32 frmid;
 	u32 chan;
 	u32 frm_len;
-	u8 frm[0];
+	u8 frm[];
 };
 
 struct GNU_PACKED classifier_header {
